---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Projects & Systems | Ayush Mishra">
  <h1>Selected Projects &amp; Systems</h1>
  <p>
    A curated collection of production-grade Machine Learning, Deep Learning, and MLOps systems built with performance, modularity, and reproducible research in mind.
  </p>

  <ul class="project-card-list">
    <!-- Project 1: Flagship Research Publication System -->
    <li class="project-card" id="fake-news-framework">
      <div class="project-header">
        <h2 class="project-title">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511/Multimodal-Fake-News-Detection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            A Unified Multimodal Fake News Detection Framework (BERT + ViT)
          </a>
        </h2>
        <div class="badge-group">
          <span class="badge badge-green">90.18% Test Acc</span>
          <span class="badge">0.9485 ROC-AUC</span>
          <span class="badge">Springer IC2NS2 '26</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-subtitle">
        Deep Learning • Multimodal Transformers • Research Publication
      </div>

      <ul class="project-highlights">
        <li>
          <strong>Core Architecture:</strong> End-to-end multimodal classification pipeline integrating <strong>BERT–BiGRU</strong> for contextual narrative semantics with a <strong>Vision Transformer (ViT-B/16)</strong> for patch-level visual representations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Empirical Outcome:</strong> Employs efficient feature concatenation fusion to achieve <strong>90.18% Test Accuracy</strong>, <strong>0.9485 ROC-AUC</strong>, and <strong>0.9084 Macro F1</strong> across 30,900 samples on the <strong>Fakeddit benchmark</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="project-footer">
        <div class="project-actions">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511/Multimodal-Fake-News-Detection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-btn project-btn-primary">
            <span>GitHub Repo</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </a>
          <button type="button" class="project-btn project-btn-secondary open-arch-modal-btn">
            <span>View Architecture SVG</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="project-btn project-btn-secondary copy-bibtex-btn" data-paper="ic2ns2_2026">
            <span>Copy BibTeX</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="project-tags">
          <span class="tech-tag">PyTorch</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">BERT-Base</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">BiGRU</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">ViT-B/16</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Feature Concatenation</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Fakeddit</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <!-- Project 2: End-to-End MLOps Pipeline -->
    <li class="project-card" id="disease-pipeline">
      <div class="project-header">
        <h2 class="project-title">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511/Poultry-Disease-Classification-MLOps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            End-to-End MLOps Disease Classification Pipeline
          </a>
        </h2>
        <div class="badge-group">
          <span class="badge badge-green">96.55% CV Acc</span>
          <span class="badge">AWS EC2</span>
          <span class="badge">Docker + DVC</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-subtitle">
        MLOps • Containerization • CI/CD • Computer Vision
      </div>

      <ul class="project-highlights">
        <li>
          <strong>Core Architecture:</strong> Production-ready automated image classification pipeline engineered for reproducible poultry disease diagnosis with modular data ingestion and validation pipelines.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Infrastructure &amp; Outcome:</strong> Attained <strong>96.55% CV accuracy</strong> with version-controlled datasets via <strong>DVC</strong>, experiment tracking using <strong>MLflow</strong>, and automated deployment to <strong>AWS EC2</strong> with <strong>Docker &amp; FastAPI</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="project-footer">
        <div class="project-actions">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511/Poultry-Disease-Classification-MLOps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-btn project-btn-primary">
            <span>Pipeline Source Code</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="project-tags">
          <span class="tech-tag">DVC</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">MLflow</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Docker</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">FastAPI</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">AWS EC2</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">GitHub Actions</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <!-- Project 3: GPUCalc -->
    <li class="project-card" id="gpucalc">
      <div class="project-header">
        <h2 class="project-title">
          <a href="https://gpu-calc.ayushmishra642001.workers.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            GPUCalc — Deep Learning &amp; LLM VRAM Sizing Engine
          </a>
        </h2>
        <div class="badge-group">
          <span class="badge badge-green">Live Tool</span>
          <span class="badge">Cloudflare Workers</span>
          <span class="badge">LLM Parallelism</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-subtitle">
        Deep Learning Infrastructure • Memory Analytics • Serverless
      </div>

      <ul class="project-highlights">
        <li>
          <strong>Core Architecture:</strong> Analytical hardware sizing and memory calculation engine designed to estimate exact GPU VRAM requirements and bandwidth bottlenecks for <strong>LLM training and inference</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Precision Sizing:</strong> Models parameter memory footprint, dynamic <strong>KV cache</strong>, activation overhead, optimizer states (<strong>AdamW / FP16 / INT8 / FP8</strong>), and multi-GPU tensor/pipeline parallelism configurations (<strong>TP / PP / DP</strong>).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="project-footer">
        <div class="project-actions">
          <a href="https://gpu-calc.ayushmishra642001.workers.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-btn project-btn-primary">
            <span>Live Demo</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511/GPUCalc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-btn project-btn-secondary">
            <span>GitHub Repo</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="project-tags">
          <span class="tech-tag">Cloudflare Workers</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Deep Learning Hardware</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">VRAM Analytics</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">LLM Inference &amp; Training</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Parallelism (TP/PP/DP)</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">JavaScript ES6+</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>

    <!-- Project 4: AllAgeCalculators.com -->
    <li class="project-card" id="all-age-calculator">
      <div class="project-header">
        <h2 class="project-title">
          <a href="https://allagecalculators.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            AllAgeCalculators.com
          </a>
        </h2>
        <div class="badge-group">
          <span class="badge badge-green">Live Web Platform</span>
          <span class="badge">Microsecond Latency</span>
          <span class="badge">SEO Optimized</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-subtitle">
        Web Platform • Chronological Analytics • High Performance
      </div>

      <ul class="project-highlights">
        <li>
          <strong>Core Architecture:</strong> Algorithmic chronological analytics platform engineered for zero-dependency client computations, dynamic chart visualizations, and responsive glassmorphism UI.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Performance &amp; Scale:</strong> Achieves microsecond client-side execution speeds, comprehensive semantic <strong>SEO optimization</strong>, and lightweight zero-bloat browser rendering.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="project-footer">
        <div class="project-actions">
          <a href="https://allagecalculators.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-btn project-btn-primary">
            <span>Live Demo</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511/AllAgeCalculators" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-btn project-btn-secondary">
            <span>GitHub Repo</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="project-tags">
          <span class="tech-tag">JavaScript ES6+</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Chronological Algorithms</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">SEO Architecture</span>
          <span class="tech-tag">Responsive Glassmorphism</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
